 "summary": "Under decision 0002, s24vmm (VM-055 --fp-on, 1 vCPU, 1 GiB) ran from tmpfs as root on the S24 with VM-002's avfboot Image and XNUP payload (xnu-8796.121.2 DEVELOPMENT BCM2837 with the owned PID 1). The console showed the Darwin banner and \"VM002: pid=1 ostype=Darwin owned-entry=v2\", and the guest ended by PSCI SYSTEM_OFF 0.29-0.67 s after start on X4 (twice), A720 and A520. A control without --fp-on hung until the 20 s timeout, as in sessions 002-004. Root cause: XNU common_start writes CPACR_EL1 with no ISB after it, and the fp-sync probe shows that an FP instruction after such a write traps on these cores. Every run removed its RAM directory, left no VMM process and did not reboot the phone. This is an XNU guest under Android KVM, not native XNU on Exynos hardware and not Apple launchd.",
